| Expected cost A | Expected cost B | Dispersion | Power |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 1.15 | 3.85 | 2.059 | 1.525 |
\image(figures/tweedie_repair_cost.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The profile peaks at a variance power of about 1.53.)
\alttext(The log likelihood rises steeply near power 1.1, peaks at 1.53, and then declines toward 1.85.)

Each point on the profile refits the mean coefficients and dispersion
at that power. The dot marks the highest fitted likelihood. The mean
costs include the shifts with zero cost.

[Dunn and Smyth, Series evaluation of Tweedie exponential dispersion model densities|https://doi.org/10.1007/s11222-005-4070-y]
